    {
      "question": "e-4684",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "59964edd96b480571cfcf5c2e5007bfdc83b4a9dd1d12ebb736e3365198e57f1",
      "new_sha256": "fd63ab08b2a3baea046cf61dfa2f20dd07a70cbb462f618be3667d9352f10b99",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-4684",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y,z$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y-3z=5 \\\\ -7x-y+z=0 \\\\ 2x+y-2z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\left\\lbrack\n\t\\matrix {\n\t\t1 & 1 & -3 \\\n\t\t-7 & -1 & 1 \\\n                2 & 1 & -2 \n\t}\n\t\\right\\rbrack\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/example-4684.json",
          "file_sha256": "9b988ce643282dd0153f1f344a76b8a500898c767740f2d2c97a9946a9c95c61"
        }
      ],
